ead  for tens of thousands of families such  questions  come too late and if current trends  persist  then many more will find themselves in  the same tragic  situation  [Music]  and i'm now joined by dw correspondent  manila children who's in delhi  uh good to see you manira so india has  just registered its biggest ever  increase in corona virus cases with more  than  270 000 in a single day  what is driving this  what exactly has triggered such a  contagious second wave which is far more  uh infectious than what we saw last year  but there are experts who are saying  that the new  mutant variant the new strain as we're  calling it has something to do with it  it is far more contagious than what we  saw  in the first wave last year but another  thing to note is that there are large  gatherings which were allowed to take  place for months  including the kommela which is one of  the largest hindu religious festivals  hundreds and thousands of people every  day were gathered in one place and after  gathering there these people have  been going back to different states in  different hometowns taking perhaps the  infections along with them  apart from that different political  parties including the bharatiya janta  party which is the national ruling party  have been organizing election rallies in  different states  so allowing such gatherings to happen  and actively organizing such  gatherings has a lot to do with why we  are in this situation  manera india is is the world's  leading maker of of raw vaccines  how is the country's own inoculation  program  doing well india had been struggling in  the past few weeks there were reports  from at least  10 states which had raised concerns that  they were running out of vaccine supply  i myself did a report last week from a  town an  hour away from the capital city of delhi  uh in which multiple hospitals had to  stop the vaccination process from  for two days and some for seven days  because they had run out of supply as  w